$DIR/main.p:5:1: //pu:stack: size 65G is larger than 64G
    //pu:stack takes a size in bytes, with an optional K, M or G suffix, from
    64K to 64G. A smaller stack leaves too little room for the runtime and the
    guard region, and a larger one does not fit the address space the runtime
    reserves. The range is a limit the language fixes.
    Use a size in range:
        //pu:stack 256M
        func main() { ... }
    (see "Implementation limits" in the Plutonium spec, section 21.4)
    (run "pluto explain E2561" for a longer explanation)
